 Anne is red, she must be smart. So Anne is smart.\n\nWait, but the statement is "Anne is not smart." If Anne is smart, then the statement is false. So the answer should be B) False.\n\nBut let me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything.\n\nAnne is rough (1), young (2). From 14, rough and young implies nice. So Anne is nice. From 18, rough and nice implies red. So Anne is red. From 16, red implies smart. So Anne is smart. Therefore, the statement "Anne is not smart" is false.\n\nI don\'t see any contradictions here. All the rules chain together to make Anne smart</think>.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
