are furry. Charlie is smart and white, so he must be furry, which aligns with fact 10.\n\nSo, I think the correct answer is A) True. Therefore, the user's initial thought of B) False might be incorrect.\n</think>\n\nThe statement \"Charlie is white\" is true based on the given context. \n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Charlie is young** (Fact 1).\n2. **Young things are nice** (Fact 12), so Charlie is nice.\n3. **Nice things are blue** (Fact 16), so Charlie is blue.\n4. **Young and blue implies smart** (Fact 9), so Charlie is smart.\n5. **Blue and smart implies furry** (Fact 10), so Charlie is furry.\n6. **Furry and nice implies white** (Fact 8), so Charlie is white.\n\nThus, the statement is true.\n\n**Answer:** A) True",
