termine if Dave is nice. Rule 16 says that all kind, cold people are nice. So, if Dave is kind and cold, then he is nice. But do we know if Dave is kind?.\n\nFrom rule 15: If someone is young, they are kind. Since Dave is young (from rule 11), he must be kind. So, Dave is kind.\n\nNow, since Dave is kind and cold, according to rule 16, he must be nice. Therefore, Dave is nice.\n\nWait, but the question is whether Dave is not nice. So, if Dave is nice, then the statement "Dave is not nice" is false.\n\nLet me double-check to make sure I didn\'t miss anything. .\n\n- Dave is cold and furry → young (rule 11).\n- Young → kind (rule 15).\n- Kind and cold → nice (rule 16).\n\nYes, that seems correct</think>.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
