adiction.\n\nTherefore, the lion is big, so the statement is true.\n\nWait, but I\'m not sure if the cow can be eaten after visiting the lion. The context doesn\'t specify the order, so it\'s possible. Therefore, the lion is big, making the statement true.\n\nBut earlier, I thought that the lion being big leads to the dog eating the cow, which contradicts the cow visiting the lion. But if the visit happens before the eating, there\'s no contradiction. So the lion is big.\n\nWait, but let me check if the cow is eaten by the dog. The cow is eaten by the bald eagle (statement 1), not the dog. So the dog eating the cow would be a separate event. So the cow is eaten by both the bald eagle and the dog? That doesn\'t make sense because the cow can\'t be eaten twice. So perhaps the dog eating the cow is a separate scenario.\n\nWait, no, the cow is eaten by the bald eagle (statement 1), so the dog can\'t eat the cow because the cow is already dead. Therefore, if the dog eats the cow, that would contradict the cow being eaten by the bald eagle. So that\'s a problem.\n\nWait, that\'s a good point. The cow is eaten by the bald eagle (statement 1), so the cow is dead. Therefore, the dog can\'t eat the cow because the cow is already dead. So if the lion is big, the dog would eat the cow, but the cow is already dead. Therefore, that\'s a contradiction because the cow can\'t be eaten by both the bald eagle and the dog.\n\nTherefore, the lion cannot be big because that would lead to the dog eating the cow, which is already eaten by the bald eagle. So the lion is not big, making the statement false.\n\nWait, that makes more sense. Because the cow is eaten by the bald eagle, the dog can\'t eat the cow. Therefore, if the lion is big, the dog would eat the cow, which is impossible because the cow is already dead. Therefore, the lion cannot be big, so the statement is false.\n\nSo, to summarize:.\n\n1. Lion is young → Lion is big (statement 21).\n2. Lion is big → Lion visits dog (statement 15).\n3. Lion visits dog → Dog eats cow (statement 17).\n4. Cow is eaten by bald eagle (statement 1) → Cow is dead.\n5. Therefore, dog can\'t eat cow because cow is already dead → Contradiction.\n6. Therefore, lion cannot be big → Lion is not big</think>.\n\nThe lion is young, which implies it is big. However, if the lion is big, it would visit the dog, causing the dog to eat the cow. But the cow is already eaten by the bald eagle, leading to a contradiction. Therefore, the lion cannot be big. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 31%|###       | 185/600 [2:52:53<38:01,  5.50s/it]
