at might affect this. For example, statement 11: If the rabbit chases the tiger, then it chases the cat. But the tiger chases the rabbit (statement 6), so the rabbit might not chase the tiger. Therefore, statement 11 doesn\'t necessarily apply. So, the rabbit chases the cat because it eats the dog, not because it chases the tiger</think>.\n\nThe rabbit chases the cat because it eats the dog, as per the given statements. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
