ght relate to Harry.\n\nPoint 4 says Harry is big. Point 6 says Harry is quiet. Point 5 says Harry is not green. Point 7 says Harry is red.\n\nFrom point 8, quiet, red people are smart. Since Harry is both quiet and red, he must be smart. Point 9 also says if someone is quiet, they are smart, which aligns with that.\n\nPoint 15 says all smart people are red, which again fits because Harry is red and smart.\n\nIs there any fact that contradicts Harry being red? Let me see. Point 5 says Harry is not green, but that doesn\'t affect his color being red. Point 14 says rough people are green, but Harry isn\'t rough because he\'s red and not green. Fiona is white, so from point 13, she\'s quiet, but that doesn\'t affect Harry.\n\nPoint 12 says if Fiona is white and red, she\'s rough. But Fiona is white, and we don\'t know if she\'s red. Since Fiona is white, from point 13, she\'s quiet. But that\'s about Fiona, not Harry.\n\nPoint 10 says if Dave is red, then he\'s big. Dave is red, so he\'s big. Point 11 says if Dave is smart and white, then he\'s big. But Dave is red, so he\'s not white, so that condition doesn\'t apply.\n\nSo, all the facts point to Harry being red</think>.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
