ind. So if someone is young and rough, they are kind, and if they are rough and kind, they are quiet.\n\nHarry is young (point 7). If Harry is rough, then from point 13, he would be kind. If he\'s rough and kind, from point 12, he would be quiet. So if Harry is rough, he is quiet.\n\nBut is Harry rough? Let\'s see. Point 15 says furry people are rough. Harry is furry (from point 9), so he must be rough. Therefore, Harry is rough.\n\nSince Harry is rough and young, from point 13, he is kind. And since he\'s rough and kind, from point 12, he is quiet.\n\nSo Harry is quiet, furry, and rough. Now, from point 11, since he\'s furry and quiet, he is round. Alternatively, from point 14, since he\'s quiet and furry, he\'s round.\n\nTherefore, Harry is round</think>.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
